WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.140
Hey, guess what? A few weeks ago, 
I finished the Esperanto skill tree on Duolingo.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:10.420
As you can see right here from the golden calf,... 
Oh! ... I mean owl, sorry.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.760
 

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.320
Hello everyone. Welcome to the LangFocus channel, 
and my name is Paul.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.920
Today, I want to talk about Duolingo.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.700
It's an application for learning languages, that now has over 100 million users.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:29.900
I've been using it for a few months,
 and it's really an effective way to learn a language.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.300
For free! 
Or, so they say.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.820
Nothing in this world comes for free,
and using Duolingo comes at a price.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.680
Quite a steep price that you need to be aware of.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.120
When using Duolingo, you sometimes
 encounter some very strange sentences.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:51.560
Some of these sentences are complete nonsense 
but others seem to be a very clear reference to the dark, 
disturbing side of human nature.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:58.140
Some people say that these sentences are just luck, 
or they result from random word combinations, 
but I beg to differ.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:02.900
There are far too many of these bizarre, 
strange translations for it to be simple luck.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.960
The truth is, Duo wants to possess your soul!

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.640
 

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.380
You don't believe me? Let me prove it to you.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:18.760
The first thing you may notice is that Duolingo is trying 
to blur the lines between human beings and animals.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.600
The bear hands the beer to a cat.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.060
The birds drink beer.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.340
Cats drink milk and beer.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.060
The duck is drinking wine.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.980
Well, by this point, you're probably imagining yourself
sitting back, having a drink with a bunch of animals,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.400
which makes you little more than a simple animal. Doesn't it?

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.800
You drink my cat's milk. 
Well, that really just is an odd statement, isn't it?

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.760
The squirrel is our captain.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.400
The girl follows the bear's example.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.900
So, humans. According to Duolingo,
you are supposed to copy what animals do.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.240
Because you should be an animal, just like them.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:53.820
I am a snake.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.720
We do not know who is human.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.960
Duolingo wants to convince you that you are the same 
as an animal. Rather than a spiritual being.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:06.040
They want you to revert back to your animal impulses, 
and your wild instincts.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:10.940
They continue this process of spiritual destruction 
by killing your self esteem.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.200
You are stupid! Well, thank you Duolingo...

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.660
You are useless.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:16.840
You eat like a pig.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:21.240
You have no culture. 
Hmm, well that's really just a low blow now, isn't it?

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.160
Now you have no friends.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.580
You have rings under your eyes.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:31.880
Yours is small. Well, yeah, it probably is a little small, 
but, you didn't have to point that out, thank you.   ( ͡° ͜ʖ ͡°)

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.640
You are just average.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.760
Sometimes I doubt your intelligence.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:42.020
Man, I am a loser. You know what, I'm kinda starting 
to feel like that after reading all these sentences.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.800
When you have no self-esteem, 
you will easily begin to hate others.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.600
 

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:53.140
What the Duo demons do next is 
make you feel contempt for other people.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:54.700
No one is good.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.440
My parents are ugly.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.280
Here's a nice, little cynical statement.
She loves him for his wealth

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.540
Your niece is stupid.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:05.720
Your parents are strange.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.720
His head is bigger than a football!
Hm... Little judgmental now, aren't we, Duolingo?

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.720
I do not like the rich. Hm...

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:17.580
Once Duolingo makes you hate yourself 
and hate other people, now you are all alone.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.100
And they are free to shape your reality.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.900
 

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:31.480
Next, they flood your mind with bizarre and grotesque imagery,
 to cut your old connection with reality, 
and begin pulling you over to the Dark Side.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.700
The bear gave birth to a duck.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:39.300
The boy eats 23 beetles. Now that's something 
I just don't want to even imagine.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.560
The engineer is in the refrigerator.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:47.840
Now I'm imagining this engineer in pieces 
in the refrigerator, so, this is getting kinda creepy.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.180
I am eating an elephant! 
Okay, poaching, eating endangered animals.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:56.900
Do you import people? 
Human trafficking, that sounds like the way to go.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.560
That is not water, it is yellow.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.720
Sorry, I'm eating a rabbit.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:05.920
The cat lays the mouse into the milk.
 What the Hell for?!

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:10.380
The kid eats insects. 
And this guy just looks so happy about that.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.100
A tiger is eating my husband.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:13.440
The wolf eats me.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:18.440
Do animals have blood? Well yes they do, but, 
we don't usually focus on it unless we have to.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:22.060
 

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:29.240
Now that you are fully open to manipulation, Duolingo 
fills you with a fascination for death and violence.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.120
How does an animal die?

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.140
I am going to die.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.680
Why is the kitchen full of blood? Well,
 that's probably because there was a double homicide.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:43.540
I am ready to die. Well, I'm not. So, please, 
don't make me repeat this sentence over and over..

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.220
You shall bleed!

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:50.560
Defeat the babies!    And exactly, 
in what context are we fighting these babies?

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:54.320
She will go to Hell. 
I'm starting to think we are all going to Hell.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:57.100
It is necessary that the husband dies.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:01.080
He has to die! And look, 
she's so happy about it, isn't murder fun?

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:08.280
Why do you have so many wounds on your body? 
Well, it could be because I have spent the last hour 
killing husbands and wild animals on Duolingo.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:13.360
Soon, they will shoot. Look how excited this woman is 
by that incoming onslaught of firepower!

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:14.800
You can die.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:17.460
We all commit crimes at times.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.180
Where were you at the time of the murder?

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:25.400
Now Duolingo knows that they're probably going to get 
you into some trouble. So they're just preparing you 
for that inevitable interrogation.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:31.120
Once your mind is filled with violence, then you are just 
a single step away from committing acts of violence.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:33.760
While Duo watches and laughs.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.040
 

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:42.720
The last step is designed to ensnare your soul 
permanently because of it's addictive nature.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:46.520
Duolingo seeks to fill your soul with sexual immorality.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.840
You must be especially careful 
when learning these sentences.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:55.340
May I kiss you? Well this one seems innocent enough, 
but, of course, it's a slippery slope.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.900
My boyfriend eats in the bedroom.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.480
The boy pleases the girls.  ( ͡° ͜ʖ ͡°)

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:03.860
Yeah, this is something we really shouldn't 
be thinking about, but, ...

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:08.160
you know, it's not that bad, 
he's pleasing them, he's making them feel good.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:14.120
You drink a man's juice. Well, no I don't, but, 
I guess there are some people out there who do.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.460
He has a big black sack.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.080
He likes balls. Well, to each his own...

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:24.980
I am not your toy. Yes, I know the feeling, 
it's kind of frustrating, isn't it?

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.820
I eat your pink strawberry. 0_0

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.180
I have zero pants!

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:36.780
Okay these cards are still bad, 
they're still obviously the work of the Devil, 
but maybe they're not as bad as the others.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.120
I guess we should still be careful though.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:42.220
The lawyer is being washed by his secretary.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:46.920
Yeah, I know this one is kinda bad, 
but, sounds kinda fun too, you know?

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:48.680
She raises her shirt.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:54.400
Yeah, sometimes women do that, um, 
I shouldn't look when they do but, you know.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.580
She takes my sugar.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.840
She wants to taste my crepes.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:04.060
You sleep between them? Well, yeah sometimes,
it's fun to sleep with multiple people.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:06.860
There's nothing dodgy there, just sleeping.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:13.620
You need to get out of here before my husband arrives.
Well, this situation sounds kinda adventurous or exciting.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:22.280
Well, so you see that Duolingo comes up with a lot of 
*interesting* sentences. Of course, it's good to be careful, 
but maybe it's not really such a big deal after all.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:24.420
Like, you have to have a sense of humor right?

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:28.080
And of course, you enjoy your life 
and seek pleasure, shouldn't you?

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:31.560
After all, you only live once and then you DIE.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:37.280
If God wanted us to be so spiritual,
why did he give us these animal instincts?

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:42.400
You know, Duolingo really is quite fun,
there's something special about it.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.740
I don't quite know what it is, but I have a special feeling 
and I don't know where it comes from.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:55.000
I just know that you should probably try Duolingo, 
very soon, and you should probably use it every day, 
as much as you can.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.680
You'll learn many things.  ( ͡° ͜ʖ ͡°)

00:07:58.420 --> 00:07:59.380
Right, Duo?

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:06.460
 

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:07.760
Thanks for watching, everyone.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:12.920
If you enjoyed this video, then please like or share it, 
especially with other fans of Duolingo.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:20.440
And if you yourself have found some interesting, funny, 
or strange sentences, inside Duolingo,
please write those in the comments down below.

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:21.900
And we'll be sure to check them out.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:24.500
Thank you for watching, have a nice day.

